1. Abstract

The Aetheris‑Secure Astrophysical Simulation Engine (ASASE‑v1.0) is a conceptual high‑performance architecture that fuses multi‑scale astrophysical simulation, native cryptographic protection, and sovereign autonomous validation into a single continuous system. It integrates N‑body gravity, relativistic magnetohydrodynamics (MHD), and thermodynamic mesh evolution with a pipelined encryption kernel and a suprakernel that mathematically validates every state transition. The core premise: computation, physics, and security are treated as one organism, not separate layers.

